2026-05-20 14:56:31,133 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-05-20 14:56:31,134 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To meet the City of Belval's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool, we can leverage our expertise in large language models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B Instruct, which is our preferred sovereign model due to its strong performance in French and self-hostable nature. This model can be fine-tuned using methods like LoRA or QLoRA to achieve domain adaptation for administrative contents and processes.

We can also utilize Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, combining retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search with our experience in vector stores like Qdrant or Weaviate. This approach will enable the tool to provide contextualized answers by effectively retrieving relevant information from a knowledge base and generating accurate responses.

To ensure efficient use of resources and reduce environmental footprint, we can apply quantization methods such as INT8 to reduce energy consumption without significantly compromising model performance. Our experience with Mistral 7B indicates that using INT8 quantization results in approximately 80% less energy usage compared to larger models like 70B models.

Furthermore, we should prioritize quarterly offline fine-tuning on anonymized data to comply with GDPR regulations and minimize the need for real-time learning from user data. This approach not only adheres to privacy requirements but also contributes to a more sustainable use of computational resources by avoiding continuous online updates.

By focusing on these technologies and methodologies, our solution can effectively support the City of Belval's administrative tasks while promoting environmentally responsible AI practices through efficient resource utilization.
